=== Part 5: the potential along and across the zero set; quadratic order ===
d=1, Z = cos(phi) + i sin(phi): ||{J0,I}||_F^2 = 0
d=1: eps^2 coeff - 8Tr(h^2) = 0 | eps^2 coeff depends on x: False | eps^4 coeff depends on x: True
      T4 analogue: [Tr(S^2)]_eps^2 - 4Tr(h^2) = 0
d=2: eps^2 coeff - 8Tr(h^2) = 0 | eps^2 coeff depends on x: False | eps^4 coeff depends on x: True
      T4 analogue: [Tr(S^2)]_eps^2 - 4Tr(h^2) = 0
d=1 straight line y=1: ||{J0,I}||^2 = 2*xs**4
d=1 curved valley y=sqrt(1-x^2): ||{J0,I}||^2 = 0

=== Part 6: conventions ===
Z = 3/5 + 4/5 i, I = omega^-1 H: I^2 = -1: True; {J0,I} = [[0, 0], [0, 0]]
Z = 3/5 + 4/5 i, I = -omega^-1 H (flipped omega): I^2 = -1: True; {J0,I} = [[0, 0], [0, 0]]
Z = 3/5 + 4/5 i, I = H^-1 omega: I^2 = -1: True; {J0,I} = [[0, 0], [0, 0]]
Z = 3/5 + 4/5 i, I = H omega: I^2 = -1: True; {J0,I} = [[0, 0], [0, 0]]
other natural polarization K0 = diag(1,-1): {K0, I[Z]} = [[-2*xg/yg, 0], [0, -2*xg/yg]] -> zero set X = 0, any Y
d=2: generic U(d)-rotated polarization J: {J,I0} = 0: True, J^2 = 1: True; kernel dim of linearized map at Z = i = 3
d=3: generic U(d)-rotated polarization J: {J,I0} = 0: True, J^2 = 1: True; kernel dim of linearized map at Z = i = 6
